r at start of each hourly tick\n- [x] `TankState` contains all top-level sub-states: geometry, environment, hardware (light/heater/filter/aeration), water, substrate layers, filter state, plant guild states, algae, microbe, microfauna, animal (shrimp), detritus, event log, RNG\n- [x] Save file is JSON containing `schema_version`, `app_version`, full `TankState`, `queued_actions`, and serialized RNG state (seed + draw count)\n- [x] `save_load_roundtrip` test: non-default seed (42), applies actions, steps 1 hour, serializes to JSON, deserializes, asserts field-by-field equality\n- [x] `determinism_basic` test: two engines with same seed (7) stepping 24 hours produce identical snapshots and full state\n- [x] `action_validation` test: negative grams → `NegativeValue`, percent 120 → `PercentOutOfRange`, fraction 1.1 → `FractionOutOfRange`, intensity -0.5 → `FractionOutOfRange`, intensity_index 1.2 → `FractionOutOfRange`, temperature 0.0 → `TemperatureTooLow`\n- [x] `action_queuing` test: RemoveShrimp(1) then AddShrimp(1) on 0 adults → result is 1 (proves insertion-order processing since reversed order would yield 0)\n- [x] Invariant checks run after every `step_hours`: non-negative mass pools, index values clamped `0.0..=1.0`, temperature > 0.0 C; event log trimmed to last 200\n- [x] `tank_data` has TOML deserialization via `serde`/`toml` with preset structs for source water, substrate, plant, shrimp, process params, and scenarios; presets loaded via `include_str!` compile-time embedding\n- [x] All preset TOML files created: source water (4), substrate (4), plants (2), shrimp (1), process params (1), scenarios (3) — all with `id`, `name`, parameters, and `[provenance]` blocks\n- [x] `open_top = false` stores configurable `lid_exchange_factor` (default `0.25`) via `TankGeometry.lid_exchange_factor` with `top_exchange_factor()` returning the factor when closed\n\n## Notes\n\nSolid Milestone 1 implementation. A few observations (none blocking):\n\n- **RNG serialization strategy**: Seed + draw-count replay is correct but O(n) on deserialization. Acceptable for v1 draw counts; the debug assertion at 2^32 draws provides a safety net.\n- **Water change dilution** correctly covers TAN, nitrite, nitrate, phosphate, DIC, DOC, DON, alkalinity, and all 7 ions — matching the future `water_change_mass_balance` test's required pools. DO is intentionally excluded (not required by that acceptance test).\n- **Source water mixing** and **temperature mixing** during water changes are acknowledged as deferred to Milestone 2. `ChangeAmbientTemperature` correctly sets `environment.ambient_temp_c` (not water temp), ready for the heat model.\n- Code is well-organized, consistently formatted, and `cargo test` passes cleanly across all 4 crates.\n\n## Commit Message\n\nfeat(tank-sim): milestone 1 — workspace skeleton, core types, RNG, save/load, and preset data"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7497,"cache_read_input_tokens":44025,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7497},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a2d92bbd-eb0a-40fc-a827-9c63436499a1","uuid":"dd2be8e4-17af-4024-bdc7-fcb7b04bb037"}
